# Reviewer-supplied real-world PDFs land in tests/data/ as a
# personal scratch dir for the developer. They are not committed
# (corpus privacy + we don't pin tests against any single sample).
# Top-level *.pdf catches the other casual scratch case too.
*.pdf
!resources/**/*.pdf
# The performance reference corpus is intentionally checked in despite
# the repo-wide *.pdf ignore (see docs/perf/corpus/README.md).
!docs/perf/corpus/*.pdf
tests/data/

# Reference screenshots produced by tools/grab_screenshots. The
# offscreen Qt platform plugin doesn't emit byte-stable PNGs across
# runs (ARGB rounding etc.), so committing them creates noisy diffs
# in unrelated PRs. Regenerate locally with `make screenshots-windows`
# (or scripts/build-windows-native.ps1 + grab_screenshots) when you
# want fresh references to drop into a PR body.
docs/screenshots/

# G2 UAT evidence screenshots. Working/throwaway captures are never
# committed — they live only in the session / PR upload flow. Per the
# 2026-07-15 inline-evidence refinement, the *curated* before/after
# captures ARE committed under docs/uat/images/ and referenced inline in
# the PR body (so the merge decision is evidence-visible). Only the
# throwaway bucket below is ignored; docs/uat/images/ is committable.
uat-screenshots/
!docs/uat/images/

# Working capture from scripts/wayland-smoke.sh (the Wayland smoke tier). The
# throwaway PNG at the repo root is regenerated on every run; the CI job
# uploads it as a build artifact instead. The one CURATED proof image is
# committed under docs/ci/images/ (which docs/** does not ignore).
/wayland-smoke.png
